      "math_academy_id": "e-9122",
      "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\textrm{Var}[X]=10$ and $\\textrm{Var}[Y]=12.$ Find $\\textrm{Var}\\left[X-2Y\\right].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX+bY]=a^2\\textrm{Var}[X]+b^2\\textrm{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}\\left[X-2Y\\right]=\\left(1\\right)^2\\cdot 10+\\left(-2\\right)^2\\cdot 12 =58.\n$$",
